{
  "title": "20: Ta-Ha طه",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰهٰ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nTAA HAA.\nTa Ha!\nمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنَ لِتَشْقٰٓى ۙ‏(2)\nMAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKAL QUR-AANA LE-TASHQAA.\nWe did not send down to you the Quran that you should be miserable,\nاِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰى ۙ‏(3)\nILLAA TAZKERATAL LEMAN-Y YAKHSHAA.\nbut only as an admonition to him who fears [his Lord].\nتَنْزِيْلًا مِّمَّنْ خَلَقَ الْاَرْضَ وَالسَّمٰوٰتِ الْعُلَى ؕ‏(4)\nTANZEELAM MIMMAN KHALAQAL ARZA WAS SAMAAWAATIL O’LAA.\nA sending down [of the Revelation] from Him who created the earth and the lofty heavens\nاَلرَّحْمٰنُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوٰى‏(5)\nRAHMAANO A’LAL A’RSHIS TAWAA.\n—the All-beneficent, settled on the Throne.\nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَمَا تَحْتَ الثَّرٰى‏(6)\nLAHU MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA MAA TAHTAS SARAA.\nTo Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, and whatever is between them, and whatever is under the ground.\nوَاِنْ تَجْهَرْ بِالْقَوْلِ فَاِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ وَاَخْفٰى‏(7)\nWA IN TAJHAR BIL-QAWLE FA-INNAHU YA’LAMUS SIRRA WA AKHFAA.\nWhether you speak loudly [or in secret tones,] He indeed knows the secret and what is still more hidden.\nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ‌ؕ لَهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى‏(8)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, LAHUL ASMAAA-UL HUSNAA.\nAllah—there is no god except Him—to Him belong the Best Names.\n‌وَهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(9)\nWA HAL ATAAKA HADEESO MOOSAA.\nDid the story of Moses come to you,\nاِذْ رَاٰ نَارًا فَقَالَ لِاَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوْۤا اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِقَبَسٍ اَوْ اَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى‏(10)\nIZ RA-AA NAARAN FA-QAALA LE-AHLEHIM KOSOO INNEE AANASTO NAARAL LA-A’LLEE AATEEKUM MINHAA BE-QABASIN AW AJEDO A’LAN NAARE HODAA.\nwhen he sighted a fire, and said to his family, ‘Wait! Indeed, I descry a fire! Maybe I will bring you a brand from it, or find some guidance at the fire.’\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَتٰٮهَا نُوْدِىَ يٰمُوْسٰىؕ‏(11)\nFALAMMAA ATAAHAA NOODEYA YAA MOOSAA.\nSo when he came to it, he was called, ‘O Moses!\nاِنِّىْۤ اَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ‌ۚ اِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًىؕ‏(12)\nINNEE ANAA RABBOKA FAKHLA’ NA’LAYK, INNAKA BIL-WAADIL MOQADDASE TOWAA.\nIndeed I am your Lord! So take off your sandals. You are indeed in the sacred valley of Tuwa.\nوَاَنَا اخْتَرْتُكَ فَاسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوْحٰى‏(13)\nWA ANAKH TARTOKA FASTAME’ LEMAA YOOHAA.\nI have chosen you; so listen to what is revealed.\nاِنَّنِىْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِىْ ۙ وَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِذِكْرِىْ‏(14)\nINNANEE ANAL LAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FA’BUDNEE, WA AQEMIS SALAATA LE-ZIKREE.\nIndeed I am Allah—there is no god except Me. So worship Me, and maintain the prayer for My remembrance.\nاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ اَكَادُ اُخْفِيْهَا لِتُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا تَسْعٰى‏(15)\nINNAS SAA-A’TA AATEYATUN AKAADO UKHFEEHAA LE-TUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA TAS-A’A.\nIndeed the Hour is bound to come: I will have it hidden, so that every soul may be rewarded for its endeavour.\nفَلَا يَصُدَّنَّكَ عَنْهَا مَنْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِهَا وَاتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ فَتَرْدٰى‏(16)\nFALAA YASUDDANNAKA A’NHAA MAL LAA YOAMENO BEHAA WAT TABA-A’ HAWAAHO FA-TARDAA.\nSo do not let yourself be distracted from it by those who do not believe in it and who follow their desires, or you will perish.’\nوَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِيْنِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(17)\nWA MAA TILKA BE-YAMEENEKA YAA MOOSAA.\n‘Moses, what is that in your right hand?’\nقَالَ هِىَ عَصَاىَ‌ۚ اَتَوَكَّؤُا عَلَيْهَا وَاَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلٰى غَنَمِىْ وَلِىَ فِيْهَا مَاٰرِبُ اُخْرٰى‏(18)\nQAALA HEYA A’SAAY, ATAWAKKA-O A’LAYHAA WA AHUSH-SHO BEHAA A’LAA GHANAMEE WA LEYA FEEHAA MA-AAREBO UKHRAA.\nHe said, ‘It is my staff. I lean on it, and with it I beat down leaves for my sheep; and I have other uses for it.’\nقَالَ اَلْقِهَا يٰمُوْسٰى‏(19)\nQAALA ALQEHAA YAA MOOSAA.\nHe said, ‘Moses, throw it down.’\nفَاَلْقٰٮهَا فَاِذَا هِىَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعٰى‏(20)\nFA-ALQAAHAA FA-EZAA HEYA HAYYATUN TAS-A’A.\nSo he threw it down, and behold, it was a snake, moving swiftly.\nقَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ‌ سَنُعِيْدُهَا سِيْرَتَهَا الْاُوْلٰى‏(21)\nQAALA KHUZHAA WA LAA TAKHAF, SANO-E’EDOHAA SEERATAHAL OOLAA.\nHe said, ‘Take hold of it, and do not fear. We will restore it to its former state.\nوَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ اِلٰى جَنَاحِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ اٰيَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(22)\nWAZ MUM YADAKA ELAA JANAAHEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAYRE SOO-IN AAYATAN UKHRAA.\nNow clasp your hand to your armpit: it will emerge white, without any harm—[this is yet] another sign,\nلِنُرِيَكَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا الْكُبْرٰى‌ۚ‏(23)\nLE-NOREYAKA MIN AAYAATENAL KUBRAA.\nthat We may show you some of Our great signs.\nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى‏(24)\nIZHAB ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\nGo to Pharaoh. He has indeed rebelled.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِىْ صَدْرِىْ ۙ‏(25)\nQAALA RABBISH RAHLEE SADREE.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Open my breast for me.\nوَيَسِّرْ لِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ ۙ‏(26)\nWA YASSIR LEE AMREE.\nMake my task easy for me.\nوَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِیْ ۙ‏(27)\nWAHLUL U’QDATAM MIN LESAANEE.\nRemove the hitch from my tongue,\nيَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِیْ ‏(28)\nYAFQAHOO QAWLEE.\n[so that] they may understand my speech.\nوَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ وَزِيْرًا مِّنْ اَهْلِىْ ۙ‏(29)\nWAJ A’L LEE WAZEERAM MIN AHLEE.\nAppoint for me a minister from my family,\nهٰرُوْنَ اَخِى ۙ‏(30)\nHAAROONA AKHEE.\nAaron, my brother.\nاشْدُدْ بِهٖۤ اَزْرِىْ ۙ‏(31)\nUSHDUD BEHI AZREE.\nStrengthen my back through him,\nوَاَشْرِكْهُ فِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ ۙ‏(32)\nWA ASHRIKHO FEE AMREE.\nand make him my associate in my task,\nكَىْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيْرًا ۙ‏(33)\nKAY NOSABBEHAKA KASEERAA.\nso that we may glorify You greatly,\nوَّنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيْرًا ؕ‏(34)\nWA NAZKORAKA KASEERAA.\nand remember You greatly.\nاِنَّكَ كُنْتَ بِنَا بَصِيْرًا‏(35)\nINNAKA KUNTA BENAA BASEERAA.\nIndeed You see us best.’\nقَالَ قَدْ اُوْتِيْتَ سُؤْلَكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(36)\nQAALA QAD OOTEETA SOALAKA YAA MOOSAA.\nHe said, ‘Moses, your request has been granted!\nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَيْكَ مَرَّةً اُخْرٰٓىۙ‏(37)\nWA LAQAD MANANNAA A’LAYKA MARRATAN UKHRAA.\nCertainly, We have done you a favour another time,\nاِذْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمِّكَ مَا يُوْحٰٓى ۙ‏(38)\nIZ AWHAYNAA ELAA UMMEKA MAA YOOHAA.\nwhen We revealed to your mother whatever was to be revealed:\nاَنِ اقْذِفِيْهِ فِى التَّابُوْتِ فَاقْذِفِيْهِ فِى الْيَمِّ فَلْيُلْقِهِ الْيَمُّ بِالسَّاحِلِ يَاْخُذْهُ عَدُوٌّ لِّىْ وَعَدُوٌّ لَّهٗ‌ ؕ وَاَلْقَيْتُ عَلَيْكَ مَحَبَّةً مِّنِّىْ ۚ وَلِتُصْنَعَ عَلٰى عَيْنِىْ ۘ‏(39)\nANIQ ZEFEEHE FIT TAABOOTE FAQZEFEEHE FIL YAMME FALYULQEHIL YAMMO BIS-SAAHELE YAAKHUZHO A’DUWWUL LEE WA A’DUWWUL LAH, WA ALQAYTO A’LAYKA MAHABBATAM MINNEE, WA LE-TUSNA-A’ A’LAA A’YNEE.\n“Put him in the casket, and cast it into the river. Then the river will cast it on the bank, and he shall be picked up by an enemy of Mine and an enemy of his.” And I made you endearing, and that you might be reared under My [watchful] eyes.\nاِذْ تَمْشِىْۤ اُخْتُكَ فَتَقُوْلُ هَلْ اَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّكْفُلُهٗ‌ ؕ فَرَجَعْنٰكَ اِلٰٓى اُمِّكَ كَىْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ ؕ وَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا فَنَجَّيْنٰكَ مِنَ الْغَمِّ وَفَتَنّٰكَ فُتُوْنًا فَلَبِثْتَ سِنِيْنَ فِىْۤ اَهْلِ مَدْيَنَ ۙ ثُمَّ جِئْتَ عَلٰى قَدَرٍ يّٰمُوْسٰى‏(40)\nIZ TAMSHEE UKHTOKA FA-TAQOOLO HAL ADULLOKUM A’LAA MAN-Y YAKFOLOH, FA-RAJA’NAAKA ELAA UMMEKA KAY TAQARRA A’YNOHAA WA LAA TAHZAN, WA QATALTA NAFSAN FA-NAJJAYNAAKA MENAL GHAMME WA FATANNAAKA FOTOONAA, FA-LABISTA SENEENA FEE AHLE MADYANA, SUMMA JEATA A’LAA QADARIN-Y YAA MOOSAA.\nWhen your sister walked up [to Pharaoh’s palace] saying, “Shall I show you someone who will take care of him?” Then We restored you to your mother, that she might not grieve and be comforted. Then you slew a soul, whereupon We delivered you from anguish, and We tried you with various ordeals. Then you stayed for several years among the people of Midian. Then you turned up as ordained, O Moses!\nوَاصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِى‌ۚ‏(41)\nWAS TANA’TOKA LE-NAFSEE.\nAnd I chose you for Myself.’\nاِذْهَبْ اَنْتَ وَاَخُوْكَ بِاٰيٰتِىْ وَلَا تَنِيَا فِىْ ذِكْرِى‌ۚ‏(42)\nIZHAB ANTA WA AKHOOKA BE-AAYAATEE WA LAA TANEYAA FEE ZIKREE.\n‘Go ahead, you and your brother, with My signs and do not flag in My remembrance.\nاِذْهَبَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى‌ ‌ۖۚ‌‌‌‏(43)\nIZHABAA ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\nBoth of you go to Pharaoh, for he has indeed rebelled.\nفَقُوْلَا لَهٗ قَوْلًا لَّيِّنًا لَّعَلَّهٗ يَتَذَكَّرُ اَوْ يَخْشٰى‏(44)\nFA-QOOLAA LAHU QAWLAL LAYYENAL LA-A’LLAHU YATAZAKKARO AW YAKHSHAA.\nSpeak to him in a soft manner; maybe he will take admonition or fear.’\nقَالَا رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّنَا نَخَافُ اَنْ يَّفْرُطَ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَوْ اَنْ يَّطْغٰى‏(45)\nQAALAA RABBANAA INNANAA NAKHAAFO AN-Y YAFROTA A’LAYNAA AW AN-Y YATGHAA.\nThey said, ‘Our Lord! We are indeed afraid that he will forestall us or will exceed all bounds.’\nقَالَ لَا تَخَافَآ‌ اِنَّنِىْ مَعَكُمَاۤ اَسْمَعُ وَاَرٰى‏(46)\nQAALA LAA TAKHAAFAA INNANEE MA-A’KOMAA ASMA-O’ WA ARAA.\nHe said, ‘Do not be afraid, for I will be with the two of you, hearing and seeing [whatever happens].\nفَاْتِيٰهُ فَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّا رَسُوْلَا رَبِّكَ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ۙ وَلَا تُعَذِّبْهُمْ‌ ؕ قَدْ جِئْنٰكَ بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌ ؕ وَالسَّلٰمُ عَلٰى مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الْهُدٰى‏(47)\nFAATEYAAHO FA-QOOLAA INNAA RASOOLAA RABBEKA FA-ARSIL MA-A’NAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA, WA LAA TO-A’ZZIBHUM, QAD JEANAAKA BE-AAYATIM MIR RABBEK, WAS SALAAMO A’LAA MANIT TABA-A’L HODAA.\nSo approach him and say, ‘‘We are the apostles of your Lord. Let the Children of Israel go with us, and do not torture them! We certainly bring you a sign from your Lord, and may peace be upon him who follows guidance!\nاِنَّا قَدْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْنَاۤ اَنَّ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰى‏(48)\nINNAA QAD OOHEYA ELAYNAA ANNAL A’ZAABA A’LAA MAN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\nIndeed it has been revealed to us that punishment shall befall those who impugn us and turn their backs [on us].’’ ’\nقَالَ فَمَنْ رَّبُّكُمَا يٰمُوْسٰى‏(49)\nQAALA FAMAR RABBOKOMAA YAA MOOSAA.\nHe said, ‘Who is your Lord, Moses?’\nقَالَ رَبُّنَا الَّذِىْۤ اَعْطٰى كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلْقَهٗ ثُمَّ هَدٰى‏(50)\nQAALA RABBONAL LAZEE A-A’TAA KULLA SHAY-IN KHALQAHU SUMMA HADAA.\nHe said, ‘Our Lord is He who gave everything its creation and then guided it.’\nقَالَ فَمَا بَالُ الْقُرُوْنِ الْاُوْلٰى‏(51)\nQAALA FAMAA BAALUL QOROONIL OOLAA.\nHe said, ‘What about the former generations?’\nقَالَ عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ رَبِّىْ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ‌‌ۚ لَا يَضِلُّ رَبِّىْ وَلَا يَنْسَى‏(52)\nQAALA I’LMOHAA I’NDA RABBEE FEE KETAAB, LAA YAZILLO RABBEE WA LAA YANSAA.\nHe said, ‘Their knowledge is with my Lord, in a Book. My Lord neither makes any error nor forgets.’\nالَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ مَهْدًا وَّسَلَكَ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا سُبُلًا وَّ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً ؕ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْ نَّبَاتٍ شَتّٰى‏(53)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA MAHDANW WA SALAKA LAKUM FEEHAA SOBOLANW WA ANZALA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AA, FA-AKHRAJNAA BEHI AZWAAJAM MIN NABAATIN SHATTAA.\nHe, who made the earth for you a cradle, and in it threaded for you ways, and sent down water from the sky, and with it We brought forth various kinds of vegetation.\nكُلُوْا وَارْعَوْا اَنْعَامَكُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى النُّهٰى‏(54)\nKOLOO WAR A’W AN-A’AMAKUM, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LE-OOLIN NOHAA.\n‘Eat and pasture your cattle.’ There are indeed signs in that for those who have sense.\nمِنْهَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ وَفِيْهَا نُعِيْدُكُمْ وَمِنْهَا نُخْرِجُكُمْ تَارَةً اُخْرٰى‏(55)\nMINHAA KHALAQNAAKUM WA FEEHAA NO-E’EDOKUM WA MINHAA NUKHREJOKUM TAARATAN UKHRAA.\nFrom it did We create you, into it shall We return you, and from it shall We bring you forth another time.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرَيْنٰهُ اٰيٰتِنَا كُلَّهَا فَكَذَّبَ وَاَبٰى‏(56)\nWA LAQAD ARAYNAAHO AAYAATENAA KULLAHAA FA-KAZZABA WA ABAA.\nCertainly We showed him all Our signs. But he denied [them] and refused [to believe them].\nقَالَ اَجِئْتَنَا لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ اَرْضِنَا بِسِحْرِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(57)\nQAALA AJEATANAA LE-TUKHREJANAA MIN ARZENAA BE-SEHREKA YAA MOOSAA.\nHe said, ‘Moses, have you come to us to expel us from our land with your magic?\nفَلَنَاْتِيَنَّكَ بِسِحْرٍ مِّثْلِهٖ فَاجْعَلْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّا نُخْلِفُهٗ نَحْنُ وَلَاۤ اَنْتَ مَكَانًا سُوًى‏(58)\nFALANAATEYANNAKA BE-SEHRIM MISLEHI FAJ-A’L BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKA MAW-E’DAL LAA NUKHLEFOHU NAHNO WA LAA ANTA MAKAANAN SOWAA.\nYet we [too] will bring you a magic like it! So fix a tryst between us and you, which neither we shall fail nor you, at a middle place.’\nقَالَ مَوْعِدُكُمْ يَوْمُ الزِّيْنَةِ وَاَنْ يُّحْشَرَ النَّاسُ ضُحًى‏(59)\nQAALA MAW-E’DOKUM YAWMUZ ZEENATE WA AN-Y YOHSHARAN NAASO ZOHAA.\nHe said, ‘Your tryst shall be the Day of Adornment, and let the people be assembled in early forenoon.’\nفَتَوَلّٰى فِرْعَوْنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيْدَهٗ ثُمَّ اَتٰى‏(60)\nFA-TAWALLAA FIR-A’WNO FA-JAMA-A’ KAYDAHU SUMMA ATAA.\nThen Pharaoh withdrew [to consult privately], summoned up his guile, and then arrived [at the scene of the contest].\nقَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى وَيْلَكُمْ لَا تَفْتَرُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا فَيُسْحِتَكُمْ بِعَذَابٍ‌ۚ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنِ افْتَرٰى‏(61)\nQAALA LAHUM MOOSAA WAYLAKUM LAA TAFTAROO A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN FA-YUSHETAKUM BE-A’ZAAB, WA QAD KHAABA MANIF TARAA.\nMoses said to them, ‘Woe to you! Do not fabricate lies against Allah, or He will obliterate you with a punishment. Whoever fabricates lies certainly fails.’\nفَتَنَازَعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّجْوٰى‏(62)\nFA-TANAAZA-O’O AMRAHUM BAYNAHUM WA ASARRUN NAJWAA.\nSo they disputed their matter among themselves, and kept their confidential talks secret.\nقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذٰٮنِ لَسٰحِرٰنِ يُرِيْدٰنِ اَنْ يُّخْرِجٰكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهِمَا وَيَذْهَبَا بِطَرِيْقَتِكُمُ الْمُثْلٰى‏(63)\nQAALOO IN HAAZAANE LA-SAAHERAANE YOREEDAANE AN-Y YUKHREJAAKUM MIN ARZEKUM BE-SEHREHEMAA WA YAZHABAA BE-TAREEQATEKOMUL MUSLAA.\nThey said, ‘These two are indeed magicians who intend to expel you from your land with their magic, and to abolish your excellent tradition!\nفَاَجْمِعُوْا كَيْدَكُمْ ثُمَّ ائْتُوْا صَفًّا‌ ۚ وَقَدْ اَفْلَحَ الْيَوْمَ مَنِ اسْتَعْلٰى‏(64)\nFA-AJME-O’O KAYDAKUM SUMMAATOO SAFFAA, WA QAD AFLAHAL YAWMA MANIS TA’LAA.\nSo summon up your ingenuity, then come in ranks. Today he who has the upper hand will be felicitous!’\nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِمَّاۤ اَنْ تُلْقِىَ وَاِمَّاۤ اَنْ نَّكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ مَنْ اَلْقٰى‏(65)\nQAALOO YAA MOOSAA IMMAA AN TULQEYA WA IMMAA AN NAKOONA AWWALA MAN ALQAA.\nThey said, ‘O Moses! Will you throw first, or shall we?’\nقَالَ بَلْ اَلْقُوْا‌ۚ فَاِذَا حِبَالُهُمْ وَعِصِيُّهُمْ يُخَيَّلُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ سِحْرِهِمْ اَنَّهَا تَسْعٰى‏(66)\nQAALA BAL ALQOO, FA-EZAA HEBAALOHUM WA E’SIYYOHUM YOKHAYYALO ELAYHE MIN SEHREHIM ANNAHAA TAS-A’A.\nHe said, ‘No, you throw first.’ Thereupon, behold, their ropes and staffs appeared to him by their magic to wriggle swiftly.\nفَاَوْجَسَ فِىْ نَفْسِهٖ خِيْفَةً مُّوْسٰى‏(67)\nFA-AWJASA FEE NAFSEHI KHEEFATAM MOOSAA.\nThen Moses felt a fear within his heart.\nقُلْنَا لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْاَعْلٰى‏(68)\nQULNAA LAA TAKHAF INNAKA ANTAL A-A’LAA.\nWe said, ‘Do not be afraid. Indeed, you will have the upper hand.\nوَاَ لْقِ مَا فِىْ يَمِيْنِكَ تَلْقَفْ مَا صَنَعُوْا‌ ؕاِنَّمَا صَنَعُوْا كَيْدُ سٰحِرٍ‌ ؕ وَلَا يُفْلِحُ السّٰحِرُ حَيْثُ اَتٰى‏(69)\nWA ALQE MAA FEE YAMEENEKA TALQAF MAA SANAO’O, INNAMAA SANAO’O KAYDO SAAHERIN, WA LAA YUFLEHUS SAAHERO HAYSO ATAA.\nThrow down what is in your right hand, and it will swallow what they have conjured. What they have conjured is only a magician’s trick, and the magician does not fare well wherever he may show up.’\nفَاُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سُجَّدًا قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ هٰرُوْنَ وَمُوْسٰى‏(70)\nFA-ULQEYAS SAHARATO SUJJADAN QAALOO AAMANNAA BE-RABBE HAAROONA WA MOOSAA.\nThereat the magicians fell down prostrating. They said, ‘We have believed in the Lord of Aaron and Moses!’\nقَالَ اٰمَنْتُمْ لَهٗ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكَبِيْرُكُمُ الَّذِىْ عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ‌ۚ فَلَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ وَّلَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ فِىْ جُذُوْعِ النَّخْلِ وَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ اَيُّنَاۤ اَشَدُّ عَذَابًا وَّاَبْقٰى‏(71)\nQAALA AAMANTUM LAHU QABLA AN AAZANA LAKUM, INNAHU LA-KABEEROKOMUL LAZEE A’LLAMAKOMUS SEHR, FALA-OQATTE-A’NNA AYDEYAKUM WA ARJOLAKUM MIN KHELAAFINW WA LA-OSALLEBANNAKUM FEE JOZOO-I’N NAKHL, WA LATA’LAMUNNA AYYONAA ASHADDO A’ZAABANW WA ABQAA.\nHe said, ‘Did you believe in him before I should permit you? He is indeed your chief who has taught you magic! Surely, I will cut off your hands and feet from opposite sides, and I will crucify you on the trunks of palm trees, and you will know which of us can inflict a severer and more lasting punishment.’\nقَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْثِرَكَ عَلٰى مَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالَّذِىْ فَطَرَنَا‌ فَاقْضِ مَاۤ اَنْتَ قَاضٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا تَقْضِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(72)\nQAALOO LAN NOASERAKA A’LAA MAA JAAA-ANAA MENAL BAYYENAATE WAL LAZEE FATARANAA FAQZE MAA ANTA QAAZ, INNAMAA TAQZEE HAAZEHIL HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nThey said, ‘We will never prefer you to the clear proofs which have come to us, and to Him who originated us. Decide whatever you want to decide. You can only decide about the life of this world.\nاِنَّاۤ اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّنَا لِيَغْفِرَ لَنَا خَطٰيٰنَا وَمَاۤ اَكْرَهْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ السِّحْرِؕ‌ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‏(73)\nINNAA AAMANNAA BE-RABBENAA LE-YAGHFERA LANAA KHATAAYAANAA WA MAA AKRAHTANAA A’LAYHE MENAS SEHR, WAL LAAHO KHAYRUNW WA ABQAA.\nWe have indeed believed in our Lord that He may forgive us our offences and the magic you compelled us to perform. Allah is better and more lasting.’\nاِنَّهٗ مَنْ يَّاْتِ رَبَّهٗ مُجْرِمًا فَاِنَّ لَهٗ جَهَنَّمَ‌ۚ لَا يَمُوْتُ فِيْهَا وَ لَا يَحْيٰى‏(74)\nINNAHU MAN-Y YAATE RABBAHU MUJREMAN FA-INNA LAHU JAHANNAM, LAA YAMOOTO FEEHAA WA LAA YAHYAA.\nWhoever comes to his Lord laden with guilt, for him shall be hell, where he will neither live nor die.\nوَمَنْ يَّاْتِهٖ مُؤْمِنًا قَدْ عَمِلَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمُ الدَّرَجٰتُ الْعُلٰىۙ‏(75)\nWA MAN-Y YAATEHI MOAMENAN QAD A’MELAS SAALEHAATE FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHOMUD DARAJAATUL O’LAA.\nBut whoever comes to Him with faith and he has done righteous deeds, for such shall be the highest ranks\nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ مَنْ تَزَكّٰى‏(76)\nJANNAATO A’DNIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, WA ZAALEKA JAZAAA-O MAN TAZAKKAA.\n—the Gardens of Eden, with streams running in them, to abide in them [forever], and that is the reward of him who keeps pure.\nوَلَقَدْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى ۙ اَنْ اَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْ فَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ طَرِيْقًا فِى الْبَحْرِ يَبَسًا ۙ لَّا تَخٰفُ دَرَكًا وَّلَا تَخْشٰى‏(77)\nWA LAQAD AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA, AN ASRE BE-E’BAADEE FAZRIB LAHUM TAREEQAN FIL BAHRE YABASAL, LAA TAKHAAFO DARAKANW WA LAA TAKHSHAA.\nWe revealed to Moses, [saying], ‘Set out with My servants at night, and strike out for them a dry path through the sea. Do not be afraid of being overtaken, and have no fear [of getting drowned].\nفَاَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ بِجُنُوْدِهٖ فَغَشِيَهُمْ مِّنَ الْيَمِّ مَا غَشِيَهُمْؕ‏(78)\nFA-ATBA-A’HUM FIR-A’WNO BE-JONOODEHI FA-GHASHEYAHUM MENAL YAMME MAA GHASHEYAHUM.\nThen Pharaoh pursued them with his troops, whereat they were engulfed by what engulfed them of the sea.\nوَاَضَلَّ فِرْعَوْنُ قَوْمَهٗ وَمَا هَدٰى‏(79)\nWA AZALLA FIR-A’WNO QAWMAHU WA MAA HADAA.\nPharaoh led his people astray and did not guide them.\nيٰبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ قَدْ اَنْجَيْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ عَدُوِّكُمْ وَوٰعَدْنٰكُمْ جَانِبَ الطُّوْرِ الْاَيْمَنَ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوٰى‏(80)\nYAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA QAD ANJAYNAAKUM MIN A’DUWWEKUM WA WAA-A’DNAAKUM JAANEBAT TOORIL AYMANA WA NAZZALNAA A’LAYKOMUL MANNA WAS SALWAA.\nO Children of Israel! We delivered you from your enemy, and We appointed with you a tryst on the right side of the Mount and We sent down to you manna and quails:\nكُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا فِيْهِ فَيَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبِىْ‌ۚ وَمَنْ يَّحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِىْ فَقَدْ هَوٰى‏(81)\nKOLOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA RAZAQNAAKUM WA LAA TATGHAW FEEHE FA-YAHILLA A’LAYKUM GHAZABEE, WA MAN-Y YAHLIL A’LAYHE GHAZABEE FAQAD HAWAA.\n‘Eat of the good things We have provided you, but do not overstep the bounds therein, lest My wrath should descend on you, and he on whom My wrath descends certainly perishes.\nوَاِنِّىْ لَغَفَّارٌ لِّمَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ثُمَّ اهْتَدٰى‏(82)\nWA INNEE LA-GHAFFAARUL LEMAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN SUMMAH TADAA.\nIndeed I forgive those who repent, become faithful, act righteously, and follow guidance.’\nوَمَاۤ اَعْجَلَكَ عَنْ قَوْمِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(83)\nWA MAA A-A’JALAKA A’N QAWMEKA YAA MOOSAA.\n[God said,] ‘O Moses, what has prompted you to hasten ahead of your people?’\nقَالَ هُمْ اُولَاۤءِ عَلٰٓى اَثَرِىْ وَ عَجِلْتُ اِلَيْكَ رَبِّ لِتَرْضٰى‏(84)\nQAALA HUM OOLAAA-E A’LAA ASAREE WA A’JILTO ELAYKA RABBE LE-TARZAA.\nHe said, ‘They are close upon my heels, and I hurried on to You, my Lord, that You may be pleased.’\nقَالَ فَاِنَّا قَدْ فَتَنَّا قَوْمَكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِكَ وَاَضَلَّهُمُ السَّامِرِىُّ‏(85)\nQAALA FA-INNAA QAD FATANNAA QAWMAKA MIM BA’DEKA WA AZALLAHOMUS SAAMERIYY.\nHe said, ‘Indeed We tried your people in your absence, and the Samiri has led them astray.’\nفَرَجَعَ مُوْسَىٰۤ اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ غَضْبَانَ اَسِفًا  ۙ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَلَمْ يَعِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا  ۙ اَفَطَالَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْعَهْدُ اَمْ اَرَدْتُّمْ اَنْ يَّحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَخْلَفْتُمْ مَّوْعِدِىْ‏(86)\nFA-RAJA-A’ MOOSAA ELAA QAWMEHI GHAZBAANA ASEFAN, QAALA YAA QAWME ALAM YA-I’DKUM RABBOKUM WA’DAN HASANAN, AFA-TAALA A’LAYKOMUL A’HDO AM ARATTUM AN-Y YAHILLA A’LAYKUM GHAZABUM MIR RABBEKUM FA-AKHLAFTUM MAW-E’DEE.\nThereupon Moses returned to his people, indignant and grieved. He said, ‘O my people! Did your Lord not give you a true promise? Did the period [of my absence] seem too long to you? Or did you desire that your Lord’s wrath should descend on you and so you failed your tryst with me?’\nقَالُوْا مَاۤ اَخْلَفْنَا مَوْعِدَكَ بِمَلْكِنَا وَلٰكِنَّا حُمِّلْنَاۤ اَوْزَارًا مِّنْ زِيْنَةِ الْقَوْمِ فَقَذَفْنٰهَا فَكَذٰلِكَ اَلْقَى السَّامِرِىُّ ۙ‏(87)\nQAALOO MAA AKHLAFNAA MAW-E’DAKA BE-MALKENAA WA LAAKINNAA HUMMILNAA AWZAARAM MIN ZEENATIL QAWME FA-QAZAFNAAHAA FAKAZAALEKA ALQAS SAAMERIYY.\nThey said, ‘We did not fail our tryst with you of our own accord, but we were laden with the weight of those people’s ornaments, and we cast them [into the fire] and so did the Samiri.’\nفَاَخْرَجَ لَهُمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَّهٗ خُوَارٌ فَقَالُوْا هٰذَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ وَاِلٰهُ مُوْسٰى  فَنَسِىَ‏(88)\nFA-AKHRAJA LAHUM I’JLAN JASADAL LAHU KHOWAARUN FA-QAALOO HAAZAA ELAAHOKUM WA ELAAHO MOOSAA FA-NASEE.\nThen he produced for them a calf—a [lifeless] body with a low—and they said, This is your god and the god of Moses, so he forgot!\nاَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَلَّا يَرْجِعُ اِلَيْهِمْ قَوْلًا ۙ وَّلَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا‏(89)\nAFALAA YARAWNA ALLAA YARJE-O’ ELAYHIM QAWLANW, WA LAA YAMLEKO LAHUM ZARRANW WA LAA NAF-A’A.\nDid they not see that it did not answer them, nor could it bring them any benefit or harm?\nوَلَقَدْ قَالَ لَهُمْ هٰرُوْنُ مِنْ قَبْلُ يٰقَوْمِ اِنَّمَا فُتِنْتُمْ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ الرَّحْمٰنُ فَاتَّبِعُوْنِىْ وَاَطِيْعُوْۤا اَمْرِىْ‏(90)\nWA LAQAD QAALA LAHUM HAAROONO MIN QABLO YAA QAWME INNAMAA FOTINTUM BEH, WA INNA RABBAKOMUR RAHMAANO FAT-TABE-O’ONEE WA ATEE-O’O AMREE.\nAaron had certainly told them earlier, ‘O my people! You are only being tested by it. Indeed your Lord is the All-beneficent. So follow me and obey my command!’\nقَالُوْا لَنْ نَّبْرَحَ عَلَيْهِ عٰكِفِيْنَ حَتّٰى يَرْجِعَ اِلَيْنَا مُوْسٰى‏(91)\nQAALOO LAN NABRAHA A’LAYHE A’AKEFEENA HATTAA YARJE-A’ ELAYNAA MOOSAA.\nThey had said, ‘We will keep on clinging to it until Moses returns to us.’\nقَالَ يٰهٰرُوْنُ مَا مَنَعَكَ اِذْ رَاَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوْٓا ۙ‏(92)\nQAALA YAA HAAROONO MAA MANA-A’KA IZ RA-AYTAHUM ZALLOO.\nHe said, ‘O Aaron! What kept you, when you saw them going astray,\nاَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ‌ؕ اَفَعَصَيْتَ اَمْرِىْ‏(93)\nALLAA TATTABE-A’N, AFA-A’SAYTA AMREE.\nfrom following me? Did you disobey my command?’\nقَالَ يَابْنَؤُمَّ لَا تَاْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِىْ وَلَا بِرَاْسِىْ‌ۚ اِنِّىْ خَشِيْتُ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِىْ‏(94)\nQAALA YAB NA-UMMA LAA TAAKHUZ BE-LEHYATEE WA LAA BE-RAASEE, INNEE KHASHEETO AN TAQOOLA FARRAQTA BAYNA BANEE ISRAAA-EELA WA LAM TARQUB QAWLEE.\nHe said, ‘O son of my mother! Do not grab my beard or my head! I feared lest you should say, ‘‘You have caused a rift among the Children of Israel and did not heed my word [of advice].’’’\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يٰسَامِرِىُّ‏(95)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBOKA YAA SAAMERIYY.\nHe said, ‘What is your business, O Samiri?’\nقَالَ بَصُرْتُ بِمَا لَمْ يَبْصُرُوْا بِهٖ فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِّنْ اَثَرِ الرَّسُوْلِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذٰلِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِىْ نَفْسِى‏(96)\nQAALA BASURTO BEMAA LAM YABSOROO BEHI FA-QABAZTO QABZATAM MIN ASARIR RASOOLE FA-NABAZTOHAA WA KAZAALEKA SAWWALAT LEE NAFSEE.\nHe said, ‘I saw what they did not see. I took a handful [of dust] from the messenger’s trail and threw it. That is how my soul prompted me.’\nقَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَاِنَّ لَكَ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ لَا مِسَاسَ‌ وَاِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّنْ تُخْلَفَهٗ‌ ۚ وَانْظُرْ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِكَ الَّذِىْ ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا‌ ؕ لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهٗ ثُمَّ لَنَنْسِفَنَّهٗ فِى الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا‏(97)\nQAALA FAZHAB FA-INNA LAKA FIL HAYAATE AN TAQOOLA LAA MESAAS, WA INNA LAKA MAW-E’DAL LAN TUKHLAFAH, WAN ZUR ELAA ELAAHEKAL LAZEE ZALTA A’LAYHE A’AKEFAA, LANOHARREQANNAHU SUMMA LANANSEFANNAHU FIL YAMME NASFAA.\nHe said, ‘Begone! It shall be your [lot] throughout life to say, ‘‘Do not touch me!’’ Indeed, there is a tryst for you which you will not fail to keep! Now look at your god to whom you went on clinging. We will burn it down and then scatter it[s ashes] into the sea.\nاِنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ؕ وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًا‏(98)\nINNAMAA ELAAHOKOMUL LAAHUL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO, WASE-A’ KULLA SHAY-IN I’LMAA.\nIndeed your God is Allah. There is no god except Him. He embraces all things in [His] knowledge.’\nكَذٰلِكَ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ مَا قَدْ سَبَقَ‌ ۚ وَقَدْ اٰتَيْنٰكَ مِنْ لَّدُنَّا ذِكْرًا ‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(99)\nKAZAALEKA NAQUSSO A’LAYKA MIN AMBAAA-E MAA QAD SABAQ, WA QAD AATAYNAAKA MIL LADUNNAA ZIKRAA.\nThus do We relate to you some accounts of what is past. Certainly, We have given you a Reminder from Ourselves.\nمَنْ اَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ فَاِنَّهٗ يَحْمِلُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وِزْرًا ۙ‏(100)\nMAN A-A’RAZA A’NHO FA-INNAHU YAHMELO YAWMAL QEYAAMATE WIZRAA.\nWhoever disregards it shall bear a burden [of punishment] on the Day of Resurrection,\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَسَآءَ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ حِمْلًا ۙ‏(101)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEH, WA SAAA-A LAHUM YAWMAL QEYAAMATE HIMLAA.\nremaining in it [forever]. Evil is their burden on the Day of Resurrection\nيَّوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ‌ وَنَحْشُرُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ يَوْمَئِذٍ زُرْقًا‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(102)\nYAWMA YUNFAKHO FIS SOORE WA NAHSHORUL MUJREMEENA YAWMA-EZIN ZURQAA.\n—the day the Trumpet will be blown; on that day We shall muster the guilty with blind eyes.\nيَّتَخَافَتُوْنَ بَيْنَهُمْ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا عَشْرًا‏(103)\nYATAKHAAFATOONA BAYNAHUM IL LABISTUM ILLAA A’SHRAA.\nThey will whisper to one another: ‘You have stayed only for ten [days].’\nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِذْ يَقُوْلُ اَمْثَلُهُمْ طَرِيْقَةً اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا يَوْمًا‏(104)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAQOOLOONA IZ YAQOOLO AMSALOHUM TAREEQATAN IL LABISTUM ILLAA YAWMAA.\nWe know best what they will say, when the smartest of them in approach will say, ‘You stayed only a day!’\nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْجِبَالِ فَقُلْ يَنْسِفُهَا رَبِّىْ نَسْفًا ۙ‏(105)\nWA YAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL JEBAALE FA-QUL YANSEFOHAA RABBEE NASFAA.\nThey question you concerning the mountains. Say, ‘My Lord will scatter them [like dust].’\nفَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًا صَفْصَفًا ۙ‏(106)\nFA-YAZAROHAA QAA-A’N SAFSAFAA.\nThen He will leave it a level plain.\nلَّا تَرٰى فِيْهَا عِوَجًا وَّلَاۤ اَمْتًا ؕ‏(107)\nLAA TARAA FEEHAA E’WAJANW WA LAA AMTAA.\nYou will not see any crookedness or unevenness in it.\nيَوْمَئِذٍ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ الدَّاعِىَ لَا عِوَجَ لَهٗ‌ؕ وَخَشَعَتِ الْاَصْوَاتُ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ فَلَا تَسْمَعُ اِلَّا هَمْسًا‏(108)\nYAWMA-EZIN-Y YATTABE-O’ONAD DAA-E’YA LAA E’WAJA LAH, WA KHASHA-A’TIL ASWAATO LIR-RAHMAANE FALAA TASMA-O’ ILLAA HAMSAA.\nOn that day they will follow the summoner without zigzagging. Their voices will be muted before the All-beneficent, and you will hear nothing but a murmur.\nيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ اِلَّا مَنْ اَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَرَضِىَ لَهٗ قَوْلًا‏(109)\nYAWMA-EZIL LAA TANFA-U’SH SHAFAA-A’TO ILLAA MAN AZENA LAHUR RAHMAANO WA RAZEYA LAHU QAWLAA.\nIntercession will not avail that day except from him whom the All-beneficent allows and approves of his word.\nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَلَا يُحِيْطُوْنَ بِهٖ عِلْمًا‏(110)\nYA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA LAA YOHEETOONA BEHI I’LMAA.\nHe knows what is before them and behind them, though they do not comprehend Him in their knowledge.\nوَعَنَتِ الْوُجُوْهُ لِلْحَىِّ الْقَيُّوْمِ‌ؕ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ حَمَلَ ظُلْمًا‏(111)\nWA A’NATIL WOJOOHO LIL-HAYYIL QAYYOOM, WA QAD KHAABA MAN HAMALA ZULMAA.\nAll faces shall be humbled before the Living One, the All-sustainer, and those who bear [the burden of] wrongdoing will fail.\nوَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَا يَخٰفُ ظُلْمًا وَّلَا هَضْمًا‏(112)\nWA MAN-Y YA’MAL MENAS SAALEHAATE WA HOWA MOAMENUN FALAA YAKHAAFO ZULMANW WA LAA HAZMAA.\nBut whoever does righteous deeds, being faithful, will neither fear any injustice or disparagement.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ قُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا وَّ صَرَّفْنَا فِيْهِ مِنَ الْوَعِيْدِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ اَوْ يُحْدِثُ لَهُمْ ذِكْرًا‏(113)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO QUR-AANAN A’RABIYYANW WA SARRAFNAA FEEHE MENAL WA-E’EDE LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOONA AW YOHDESO LAHUM ZIKRAA.\nThus We have sent it down as an Arabic Quran and We have paraphrased the warnings in it variously so that they may be Godwary, or it may prompt them to remembrance.\nفَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ‌ ۚ وَلَا تَعْجَلْ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يُّقْضٰٓى اِلَيْكَ وَحْيُهٗ‌ وَقُلْ رَّبِّ زِدْنِىْ عِلْمًا‏(114)\nFA-TA-A’ALAL LAAHUL MALEKUL HAQ, WA LAA TA’JAL BIL-QUR-AANE MIN QABLE AN-Y YUQZAA ELAYKA WAHYOH, WA QUR RABBE ZIDNEE I’LMAA.\nSo exalted is Allah, the True Sovereign. Do not hasten with the Quran before its revelation is completed for you, and say, ‘My Lord! Increase me in knowledge.’\nوَلَقَدْ عَهِدْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اٰدَمَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَنَسِىَ وَلَمْ نَجِدْ لَهٗ عَزْمًا‏(115)\nWA LAQAD A’HIDNAA ELAA AADAMA MIN QABLO FA-NASEYA WA LAM NAJID LAHU A’ZMAA.\nCertainly We had enjoined Adam earlier; but he forgot, and We did not find any resoluteness in him.\nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اَبٰى‏(116)\nWA IZ QULNAA LIL-MALAAA-EKATIS JODOO LE-AADAMA FA-SAJADOO ILLAA IBLEES, ABAA.\nWhen We said to the angels, ‘Prostrate before Adam,’ they prostrated, but not Iblis: he refused.\nفَقُلْنَا يٰۤاٰدَمُ اِنَّ هٰذَا عَدُوٌّ لَّكَ وَلِزَوْجِكَ فَلَا يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقٰى‏(117)\nFA-QULNAA YAA AADAMO INNA HAAZAA A’DUWWUL LAKA WA LE-ZAWJEKA FALAA YUKHREJANNAKOMAA MENAL JANNATE FA-TASHQAA.\nWe said, ‘O Adam! This is indeed an enemy of yours and your mate’s. So do not let him expel you from paradise, or you will be miserable.\nاِنَّ لَكَ اَلَّا تَجُوْعَ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَعْرٰىۙ‏(118)\nINNA LAKA ALLAA TAJOO-A’ FEEHAA WA LAA TA’RAA.\nYou will neither be hungry in it nor naked.\nوَاَنَّكَ لَا تَظْمَؤُا فِيْهَا وَلَا تَضْحٰى‏(119)\nWA ANNAKA LAA TAZMA-O FEEHAA WA LAA TAZHAA.\nYou will neither be thirsty in it, nor suffer from [the heat of] the sun.’\nفَوَسْوَسَ اِلَيْهِ الشَّيْطٰنُ قَالَ يٰۤاٰدَمُ هَلْ اَدُلُّكَ عَلٰى شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَّا يَبْلٰى‏(120)\nFA-WASWASA ELAYHISH SHAYTAANO QAALA YAA AADAMO HAL ADULLOKA A’LAA SHAJARATIL KHULDE WA MULKIL LAA YABLAA.\nThen Satan tempted him. He said, ‘O Adam! Shall I show you the tree of immortality, and an imperishable kingdom?’\nفَاَكَلَا مِنْهَا فَبَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْاٰ تُہُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفٰنِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِنْ وَّرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ‌ وَعَصٰۤى اٰدَمُ رَبَّهٗ فَغَوٰى‌ۖ‏(121)\nFA-AKALAA MINHAA FA-BADAT LAHOMAA SAW-AATOHOMAA WA TAFEQAA YAKHSEFAANE A’LAYHEMAA MINW WARAQIL JANNAH, WA A’SAA AADAMO RABBAHU FA-GHAWAA.\nSo they both ate of it, and their nakedness became evident to them, and they began to stitch over themselves with the leaves of paradise. Adam disobeyed his Lord, and went amiss.\nثُمَّ اجْتَبٰهُ رَبُّهٗ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ وَهَدٰى‏(122)\nSUMMAJ TABAAHO RABBOHU FA-TAABA A’LAYHE WA HADAA.\nThen his Lord chose him, and turned to him clemently, and guided him.\nقَالَ اهْبِطَا مِنْهَا جَمِيْعًا‌ۢ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ‌ ۚ فَاِمَّا يَاْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِّنِّىْ هُدًى ۙ فَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ هُدَاىَ فَلَا يَضِلُّ وَلَا يَشْقٰى‏(123)\nQAALAH BETAA MINHAA JAMEE-A’M BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN A’DUWW, FA-IMMAA YAATEYANNAKUM MINNEE HODAN, FAMANIT TABA-A’ HODAAYA FALAA YAZILLO WA LAA YASHQAA.\nHe said, ‘Get down both of you from it, all together, being enemies of one another! Yet, should any guidance come to you from Me, those who follow My guidance will not go astray, nor will they be miserable.\nوَمَنْ اَعْرَضَ عَنْ ذِكْرِىْ فَاِنَّ لَهٗ مَعِيْشَةً ضَنْكًا وَّنَحْشُرُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَعْمٰى‏(124)\nWA MAN A-A’RAZA A’N ZIKREE FA-INNA LAHU MA-E’ESHATAN ZANKANW WA NAHSHOROHU YAWMAL QEYAAMATE A-A’MAA.\nBut whoever disregards My remembrance, his shall be a wretched life, and We shall raise him blind on the Day of Resurrection.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ لِمَ حَشَرْتَنِىْۤ اَعْمٰى وَقَدْ كُنْتُ بَصِيْرًا‏(125)\nQAALA RABBE LEMA HASHARTANEE A-A’MAA WA QAD KUNTO BASEERAA.\nHe will say, ‘My Lord! Why have You raised me blind, though I used to see?’\nقَالَ كَذٰلِكَ اَتَتْكَ اٰيٰتُنَا فَنَسِيْتَهَا‌ۚ وَكَذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمَ تُنْسٰى‏(126)\nQAALA KAZAALEKA ATATKA AAYAATONAA FA-NASEETAHAA, WA KAZAALEKAL YAWMA TUNSAA.\nHe will say: ‘So it is. Our signs came to you, but you forgot them, and so you will be forgotten today.’\nوَكَذٰلِكَ نَجزِىْ مَنْ اَسْرَفَ وَلَمْ يُؤْمِنْۢ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَشَدُّ وَاَبْقٰى‏(127)\nWA KAZAALEKA NAJZEE MAN ASRAFA WA LAM YOAMIM BE-AAYAATE RABBEH, WA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE ASHADDO WA ABQAA.\nThus do We requite those who transgress and do not believe in the signs of their Lord, and the punishment of the Hereafter is severer and more lasting.\nاَفَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ يَمْشُوْنَ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى النُّهٰى‏(128)\nAFALAM YAHDE LAHUM KAM AHLAKNAA QABLAHUM MENAL QOROONE YAMSHOONA FEE MASAAKENEHIM, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LE-OOLIN NOHAA.\nDoes it not dawn upon them how many generations We have destroyed before them, amid [the ruins of] whose dwellings they walk? There are indeed signs in this for those who have reason.\nوَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَكَانَ لِزَامًا وَّاَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّىؕ‏(129)\nWA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIR RABBEKA LAKAANA LEZAAMANW WA AJALUM MOSAMMAA.\nWere it not for a prior decree of your Lord and a specified time, [their doom] would have attended [their guilt].\nفَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوْعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ غُرُوْبِهَا‌ ۚ وَمِنْ اٰنَآئِ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْ وَاَطْرَافَ النَّهَارِ لَعَلَّكَ تَرْضٰى‏(130)\nFASBIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WA SABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA QABLA TOLOO-I’SH SHAMSE WA QABLA GHOROOBEHAA, WA MIN AANAAA-IL LAYLE FA-SABBEH WA ATRAAFAN NAHAARE LA-A’LLAKA TARZAA.\nSo be patient with what they say, and celebrate the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the sunset, and glorify Him in watches of the night and at the day’s ends, that you may be pleased.\nوَلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ اِلٰى مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْهُمْ زَهْرَةَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ لِنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَرِزْقُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‏(131)\nWA LAA TAMUDDANNA A’YNAYKA ELAA MAA MATTA’NAA BEHI AZWAAJAM MINHUM ZAHRATAL HAYAATID DUNYAA, LE-NAFTENAHUM FEEH, WA RIZQO RABBEKA KHAYRUNW WA ABQAA.\nDo not extend your glance toward what We have provided certain groups of them as a glitter of the life of this world, so that We may test them thereby. The provision of your Lord is better and more lasting.\nوَاْمُرْ اَهْلَكَ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَاصْطَبِرْ عَلَيْهَا‌ ؕ لَا نَسْئَلُكَ رِزْقًا‌ ؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكَ‌ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلتَّقْوٰى‏(132)\nWAAMUR AHLAKA BIS-SALAATE WAS TABIR A’LAYHAA, LAA NAS-ALOKA RIZQAA, NAHNO NARZOQOK, WAL A’AQEBATO LIT-TAQWAA.\nAnd bid your family to prayer and be steadfast in maintaining it. We do not ask any provision of you: it is We who provide for you, and to Godwariness belongs the ultimate outcome [in the Hereafter].\nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَا يَاْتِيْنَا بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ ‌ؕ اَوَلَمْ تَاْتِہِمْ بَيِّنَةُ مَا فِى الصُّحُفِ الْاُوْلٰى‏(133)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA YAATEENAA BE-AAYATIM MIR RABBEH, AWA LAM TAATEHIM BAYYENATO MAA FIS SOHOFIL OOLAA.\nThey say, ‘Why does he not bring us a sign from his Lord?’ Has there not come to them a clear proof in that which is in the former scriptures?\nوَلَوْ اَنَّاۤ اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لَوْلَاۤ اَرْسَلْتَ اِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا فَنَتَّبِعَ اٰيٰتِكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ نَّذِلَّ وَنَخْزٰى‏(134)\nWA LAW ANNAA AHLAKNAAHUM BE-A’ZAABIM MIN QABLEHI LAQAALOO RABBANAA LAWLAA ARSALTA ELAYNAA RASOOLAN FA-NATTABE-A’ AAYAATEKA MIN QABLE AN NAZILLA WA NAKHZAA.\nHad We destroyed them with a punishment before it, they would have surely said, ‘Our Lord! Why did You not send us an apostle so that we might have followed Your signs before we were abased and disgraced?’\nقُلْ كُلٌّ مُّتَرَبِّصٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوْا‌ ۚ فَسَتَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ اَصْحٰبُ الصِّرَاطِ السَّوِىِّ وَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(135)\nQUL KULLUM MOTARABBESUN FA-TARABBASOO, FASATA’LAMOONA MAN ASHAABUS SERAATIS SAWIYYE WA MANEH TADAA.\nSay, ‘Everyone [of us] is waiting. So wait! Soon you will know who are the people of the right path, and who is [rightly] guided.’",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has 135 verses. It is mentioned in a narration from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah will get the reward equivalent to the number of companions of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) from the Mohaajereen and Ansaar.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that Allah (s.w.t.) befriends the ones who recite this Surah and this person will receive his book of deeds on his right hand. His sins will be forgiven and he will get so much reward that he will be pleased on the Day of Judgement.\nThis Surah should be recited before war, going before a tyrant ruler and trying to guide a community towards the path of Allah (s.w.t.). If a girl is not getting married and she wishes to get married, she should take ghusl (bath) with water in which this Surah has been dissolved and by the will of Allah (s.w.t.) she will get married.\nIf a man wishes to get married, he should write verses 131 and 132 of this Surah with saffron and then wear it as a talisman and Inshallah his proposal will be accepted."
